  "eyebrow": "Plan review",
  "title": "A read-through cache for the catalog",
  "subtitle": "Proposal: put Redis in front of product reads and invalidate on write.",
  "change": { "title": "Illustrative plan, not a real system" },
  "summary": "Product pages read the catalog database on every request, and the read path is most of the database load. The plan adds a **read-through cache**: handlers ask Redis first, fall back to Postgres on a miss, and admin writes delete the affected keys. The risk is stale data; the plan bounds it with a TTL and explicit invalidation.",
